            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Previous studies suggest that nuclear histone deacetylase HDAC5 has a dynamic relationship with drug-induced behavioral neuroadaptations. The new work by Taniguchi et al. (2017) suggests that targets of nuclear HDAC5 mediate the behavioral effects of rewarding drugs via regulation of cocaine-associated stimuli.</AbstractText>
